// Flag bits by group: `ck(FG_COMMON, F_COMMON_INTRO_SEEN, TRUE)`.
// F_<group>_<bit> is a bit not yet named; a room's own FG_ROOM bits are
// defined in its script. Named bits say what they mean when set:
// - F_ITEM_<room>_<item>_<model>: the pickup with that IT_ name (less its
//   id) and IMDL slot, set while it is still there;
// - F_ENEMY_<room>_<type>_<slot>: the enemy with that EM_ name (less its id)
//   in that room's ENEMY_ slot, set once it is dead;
// - F_LOCK_<room>_<room>: the door between the two rooms, set once unlocked;
// - _J_ / _C_ after the group: the bit means this only in Jill's / Chris's
//   game. A bit both games use for different things has a define for each,
//   and each use takes the name of its player's branch.

#define F_SCENARIO_STAGE_VARIANT 0x00                       // Stage changes go to the +5 stage variants while set (engine).
